  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A tertiary alkyl halide with strong base undergoes elimination reaction, while a primary alkyl halide with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>-</mo></math>butoxide gives ether by a substitution reaction.&nbsp;<meta name=\"uuid\" content=\"uuidBj8xLkcWhcrj\" /><meta charset=\"utf-8\" />Alkenes undergo hydration (addition of water) by Hydroboration-Oxidation, giving anti-Markovnikov&#39;s products and by Oxymercuration-Demercuration, giving&nbsp;Markovnikov&#39;s&nbsp;products.<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EM0012657_AnsExp4_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 665px; height: 319px;\" /></p>",
